    "Full API spec": "Module: include/Record.h (and src/Record.cpp)\n- Type: struct Record\n  - Public fields: std::string id; std::string name; std::string email; std::uint64_t revision; std::uint64_t updated_at.\n  - Constructor: Record(std::string id, std::string name, std::string email, std::uint64_t revision, std::uint64_t updated_at);\n    Semantics: initializes all fields exactly as provided; no default constructor provided.\n  - bool operator==(const Record& other) const;\n    Semantics: returns true iff all five fields are equal by value.\n  - Includes: <cstdint>, <string>.\n\nModule: include/ManualClock.h (and src/ManualClock.cpp)\n- Type: class ManualClock\n  - explicit ManualClock(std::uint64_t initial);\n    Semantics: initializes internal counter to 'initial'. No wall-clock usage. Declared only in header; defined only in src/ManualClock.cpp.\n  - std::uint64_t now() const noexcept;\n    Semantics: returns current counter value.\n  - void advance(std::uint64_t delta) noexcept;\n    Semantics: increments internal counter by 'delta'. No overflow checks required by contract; caller responsibility.\n  - Includes: <cstdint>.\n\nModule: include/Repository.h (and src/Repository.cpp)\n- Type: class Repository (concrete in-memory repository)\n  - Private: std::map<std::string, Record> records_;\n  - bool insert(const Record& rec);\n    Return: true if id was absent and rec inserted; false if id already exists (no mutation).\n  - std::optional<Record> find(const std::string& id) const;\n    Return: a copy of the Record if present; std::nullopt otherwise.\n  - bool replace(const Record& rec);\n    Return: true if an existing record with same id was present and replaced; false if absent (no insertion).\n  - bool erase(const std::string& id);\n    Return: true if an element was erased; false if nothing erased.\n  - std::vector<Record> list() const;\n    Return: vector of all records in deterministic std::map key order (lexicographic by id).\n  - Includes: <map>, <optional>, <string>, <vector>, and \"Record.h\".\n\nModule: include/CrudService.h (and src/CrudService.cpp)\n- Type: class CrudService\n  - Private refs: Repository& repository_; ManualClock& clock_.\n  - CrudService(Repository& repository, ManualClock& clock);\n    Semantics: stores references; no ownership; no null allowed (references).\n  - Record create(const std::string& id, const std::string& name, const std::string& email);\n    Validation: throws std::invalid_argument if id or name is blank (empty or all spaces handled by caller; at minimum empty disallowed) or if email does not contain exactly one '@' not at the first or last character.\n    Duplicate: throws std::runtime_error if insert fails due to existing id.\n    State: constructs Record{id, name, email, revision=1, updated_at=clock_.now()} and inserts via repository_. Returns the stored Record.\n  - std::optional<Record> get(const std::string& id) const;\n    Semantics: returns repository_.find(id).\n  - Record update(const std::string& id, const std::string& name, const std::string& email);\n    Validation: same as create for name/email; id must be non-blank.\n    Absent: throws std::runtime_error if target id does not exist.\n    State: reads existing record, preserves id, increments revision by one (prev.revision + 1), sets updated_at to clock_.now(), and replaces via repository_. Returns the new record.\n  - bool remove(const std::string& id);\n    Semantics: returns repository_.erase(id).\n  - std::vector<Record> list() const;\n    Semantics: returns repository_.list(); deterministic order by id.\n  - Includes: <optional>, <string>, <vector>, \"ManualClock.h\", \"Record.h\", and \"Repository.h\".\n\nModule: src/Main.cpp\n- Runtime entry: constructs Repository repo; ManualClock clock(100); CrudService service(repo, clock); creates Record with id \"1\"; prints at most one concise value; returns 0. No loops, no wall clock.\n\nAllowed include direction:\n- Headers are self-contained and include only what they use.\n- CrudService.h may include ManualClock.h, Record.h, Repository.h.\n- Repository.h includes Record.h.\n- Tests include only headers from include/ by basename in code (e.g., \"CrudService.h\").\n- Sources include their corresponding headers by basename only; no transitive reliance on standard headers.\n\nExceptions and validation rules:\n- std::invalid_argument for invalid inputs: blank id/name or malformed email (must contain exactly one '@' not at edges).\n- std::runtime_error for duplicate create or absent update.\n- ManualClock operations are noexcept and deterministic.\n\nDeterministic behaviors:\n- ManualClock is the sole time source; now() used for updated_at in create/update.\n- Repository list() order is deterministic by std::map key.\n\nNotes:\n- Constructor declarations appear only in headers; definitions only in matching .cpp files.\n- No extra files, interfaces, or namespaces are allowed.",
    "Shared Knowledge": "Exactly 11 files form the project: CMakeLists.txt; include/Record.h; src/Record.cpp; include/ManualClock.h; src/ManualClock.cpp; include/Repository.h; src/Repository.cpp; include/CrudService.h; src/CrudService.cpp; src/Main.cpp; tests/test_main.cpp. Headers are self-contained and use #pragma once with explicit standard includes: Record.h (<cstdint>, <string>); ManualClock.h (<cstdint>); Repository.h (<map>, <optional>, <string>, <vector>, and \"Record.h\"); CrudService.h (<optional>, <string>, <vector>, \"ManualClock.h\", \"Record.h\", and \"Repository.h\"). Sources include headers by basename only. CMake builds a static core library (crud_core) from the four core .cpp files and links both runtime (crud_app) and test (crud_tests) executables to it. tests/test_main.cpp includes only headers (\"CrudService.h\") plus standard headers and defines exactly one main with three blocks.",
